  "status": "published_open",
  "body": "### Description\n\n`prepare_all_predictions` invokes LightFM separately for every retained user/item pair, repeating native feature construction and input checks. Its interaction lookup also uses row-wise DataFrame callbacks.\n\nRead the pair weights with sparse indexing and pass the retained int32 ID arrays to a single native `predict` call. Preserve the existing `rating < 1` rule, external IDs, user/item ordering, float32 scores, optional user/item features and thread setting. An empty retained set now returns the expected empty schema.\n\nFixes #2479.\n\n### Native validation\n\n[Independent validation](https://github.com/Afloat16/recommenders/actions/runs/43918605411) checks exact head `9db933e55ff92a527fe5fbb1bb06f5bc27724abd` with official LightFM 1.17 on both Python 3.10/NumPy 1.24.4/SciPy 1.10.1 and Python 3.11/NumPy 1.26.4/SciPy 1.13.1.\n\n- Original suite: **4 passed, 1 existing skip**.\n- New cases on baseline: **6 failed, 16 passed**. The failures are empty-data, all-seen and single-seen selections, with and without features.\n- Patched full suite: **26 passed, 1 existing skip** on both environments and local Python 3.12.\n- Black and `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nThe existing flaky `test_fitting` remains the only skip. All new cases run against native fitted models. Complete DataFrames match individual native predictions exactly, including pair order and dtypes. Coverage includes all four user/item feature combinations, one/two threads, COO/CSR inputs, duplicate sparse coordinates, fractional/negative interaction weights, and unchanged caller data.\n\n### Complete-function benchmark\n\nFive alternating timed calls per implementation, after warmup, with the same rank-8 fitted WARP model and one CPU thread. Every output DataFrame is checked for exact equality; score digests also match across environments.\n\n| Users \u00d7 items | Optional features | Retained pairs | Python 3.11 before \u2192 after (median) | Python 3.11 speedup | Python 3.10 speedup |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 40 \u00d7 40 | No | 1,470 | 110.68 \u2192 1.68 ms | 65.96\u00d7 | 73.90\u00d7 |\n| 40 \u00d7 40 | Yes | 1,470 | 57.06 \u2192 1.75 ms | 32.56\u00d7 | 35.39\u00d7 |\n| 100 \u00d7 150 | No | 13,827 | 1,011.53 \u2192 5.05 ms | 200.47\u00d7 | 263.64\u00d7 |\n| 100 \u00d7 150 | Yes | 13,827 | 509.68 \u2192 5.70 ms | 89.49\u00d7 | 104.01\u00d7 |\n\nThese measurements cover the full `prepare_all_predictions` helper on the stated synthetic inputs, not model training or an entire application. The reproducible benchmark, dependency versions and raw samples are in the validation artifacts.\n\n### History review\n\nReviewed 1,497 pre-existing upstream PR heads, 69 fork branches and all 28 reachable utility source versions across 110 commits, including former paths and intermediate revisions. All four historical prediction variants make per-pair calls. Earlier #1611, #1624 and #1651 fix ID types; #2272/#2273 optimize the separate test-data preparation helper.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] Contribution guidelines and code style followed.\n- [x] Native compatibility and regression cases added to the existing LightFM module.\n- [x] Commit includes the required `Signed-off-by` trailer.\n- [x] Targets `staging`.\n",
